{{also|pus}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|cat, woman, vulva; mouth, face}}<!--but presumably not the sense "pus" which rhymes with cuss, fuss!--> {{enPR|po͝os}}, {{IPA|en|/pʊs/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-puss.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊs|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{der|en|gml|pūs}}, {{m|gml|pūskatte}} or {{der|en|nl|poes||puss, cat”, slang for “vulva}}, ultimately from a common {{der|en|gem}} word for cat, perhaps ultimately {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}} of a sound made to get its attention (compare Arabic [[بسة]] (bissa)).

Akin to {{cog|fy|poes}}, {{cog|nds|Puus}}, {{m|nds|Puuskatte}}, {{cog|da|pus}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|kattepus}}, {{cog|no|pus}}.

Found also in several other European, North African and Asian languages; compare {{cog|ro|pisică}}, {{cog|fa|پیشی|tr=''piši''}}, {{cog|ta|பூசை}}, {{cog|tl|pusa}}
and {{cog|sc|pisittu}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|informal|often as a term of address}} A [[cat]].
#: {{ux|en|Our local theatre is showing '''''Puss''' in Boots''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Come here, '''puss'''! I've got some milk for you.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|affectionate}} A [[girl]] or young [[woman]], or any [[child]].
# {{lb|en|dated|hunting}} A [[hare]].
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|volume=II|book=V|chapter=In which is seen a more moving Spectacle, than all the Blood in the Bodies of ''Thwackum'' and ''Blifil'' and of Twenty other such, is capable of producing|page=220|passage=He then began to beat about, in the ſame Language, and in the ſame Manner, as if he had been beating for a Hare, and at laſt cried out, 'Soho! '''Puſs''' is not far off. Here's her Form, upon my Soul; I believe I may cry ''ſtole away''.'}}
#* {{RQ:Asbjornsen Braekstad Tales|chapter=A Day with the Capercailzies|page=77|passage='{{...|nospace=1}} It won't kill '''Puss''' any better for that.' / "'But, goodness gracious, what can that hare be made of?' I asked.}}
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} The [[vulva]] (female [[genitalia]]).
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|slang|metonymic}} [[sex|Sex]] with a woman.
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1986|writers=Tim Kazurinsky; Denise DeClue|title={{w|About Last Night (1986 film)|About Last Night}}|role=Bernie|actor=Jim Belushi|passage=So don't know! So, what are you gonna do? Sell your birthright for a little bit of '''puss'''?}}
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang|chiefly|_|North America}} A [[coward]]; a [[wuss]]; someone who is unable to stand up for themselves.

